\section{The Proof of Theorem \ref{tp4spec}}\label{mainpf}
Let $e(A,B)$ denote the number of edges in $G$ with one end in $A$ and the other in $B$. In addition, we simply write $e(A,A)$ as $e(A)$. For a vertex $v\in V(G)$, define $A=N(v)$, $B=N_2(v)$ and $C=V(G)\setminus(A\cup B\cup\{v\})$. 
We have the following fact. 
\begin{fact}\label{fact1}
  If $d(w)\geq 2$ for any $w\in N_2(v)$, then $$\sum_{w\in N_2(v)}|N(w)\cap N(v)| \cdot d(w)-2e(A,B)\geq 0,$$ where equality holds if and only if $d(w)=2$ for any $w\in N_2(v)$.    
